<title>FRANCE: AGF hopes 1996 result will be twice H1.</title>
<headline>AGF hopes 1996 result will be twice H1.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Insurer Assurances Generales de France (AGF) aims to post a full-year result for 1996 twice the first-half figure, chairman Antoine Jeancourt-Galignani said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are trying to make about double the first-half figure, but for that to happen there should be no bad surprises,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
<p>AGF reported a first-half net attributable profit of 723 million francs up from 487 million. In 1995, it posted a 23 percent increase to 1.08 billion.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
